      "act": "COLD OPEN — THE WRITER",
      "lane": "TERMINAL",
      "narration_text": "This is Liam, in for Bear. One sentence: write a script that prints pass or fail for our study group. Five rows, a couple of them awkward on purpose. It reads the file, decides how missing scores should count, and writes eleven lines of Python. Runs it. Five students. Three passes, two fails. Now — is that right? Ask the same session to review its own code. Same model. Same weights. Watch which questions it can ask and which it can't.",
      "estimated_duration_s": 28.8,
      "voice": "am_onyx",
      "engine": "kokoro",
      "voice_kokoro": "am_onyx",
